cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ulap Digital Twin: a 6G propagation study pipeline"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Zoe Aiyanna M."
    family-names: Cayetano
    affiliation: "Amini Labs"
  - given-names: "George M."
    family-names: Gichuru
    affiliation: "Amini Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aminitech/aminiulap-digital-twin"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end pipeline for building geospatially accurate digital twins and
  running 6G radio propagation studies over them. Clips authoritative
  geospatial layers to a study area, builds a textured 3D scene in Blender,
  exports it to Mitsuba, and runs ray-traced coverage, path gain, and SINR
  analyses in NVIDIA Sionna. Includes an interactive study wizard that lets a
  user define a new study area anywhere in the world from open data sources.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - 6G
  - ISAC
  - radio propagation
  - ray tracing
  - Sionna
  - Mitsuba
  - geospatial
  - small island developing states
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release archiving (ULAP-15)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Zenodo mints a DOI when a GitHub *release* is published, and it can only see
# PUBLIC repositories — so this stays commented until the repo is public and a
# release is tagged. Two DOIs come back: a version DOI for that specific release
# and a concept DOI that always resolves to the newest version. Cite the version
# DOI in a paper; a reader must be able to get the exact tree the numbers came
# from.
#
# Uncomment and fill from the Zenodo record:
#
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX        # version DOI for this release
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX  # concept DOI — resolves to latest version
#     description: "Concept DOI (all versions)"
#
# The accompanying paper is not yet announced on arXiv. Once it is, replace the
# placeholder below with the real eprint id and DOI, and mirror the change in
# research-paper/README.md.
#
# references:
#   - type: article
#     title: "Sovereign Cognitive Digital Twins: Fusing 6G ISAC, AI-RAN, and Zero-Trust Edge Grids"
#     authors:
#       - given-names: "Zoe Aiyanna M."
#         family-names: Cayetano
#       - given-names: Taijuo
#         family-names: Morris
#       - given-names: "George M."
#         family-names: Gichuru
#     year: 2026
#     identifiers:
#       - type: other
#         value: "arXiv:TODO"
